{
    "background_story": "Isaac Steffens was a renowned paleontologist, famous for his groundbreaking discoveries in the field of dinosaur research. Growing up in a family of scientists, Isaac was fascinated by the ancient creatures that once roamed the earth. He spent years studying the works of his idol, the great paleontologist Roy Chapman Andrews. Isaac's own research led him to a remarkable find in the badlands of Montana - a nearly complete T-Rex skeleton, later named 'Steffens' Rex' in his honor. The discovery sparked a new wave of interest in paleontology, and Isaac became a celebrated figure in the scientific community. He continued to explore the mysteries of the prehistoric world, inspiring a new generation of scientists to follow in his footsteps.",
